.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    See whether last finalized assignment ratings are trustworthy — employee, manager, and final agreement — so talent density isn’t built on soft or unclear data.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  %p.mb-3
    Emp≠mgr is a clarity signal. Finals that always take the manager or employee amplify leniency or expectation gaps. This view is for coaching discussion, not shaming. Nobody sees their own marker.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %ul.mb-0
    %li Y-axis is assignments held by people in the current filter.
    %li X-axis is how emp / mgr / final lined up on each person’s last finalized check-in for that assignment.
    %li Arrows show direction when useful: final vs manager in most disagreement columns; final vs employee when mgr+final matched and emp differed (rated higher / rated lower). No arrow when all three match.
    %li Filters above the tabs are shared with Stances and the other matrices.
